    "done_when": "telemetry_ingest.run catches sqlite3.OperationalError whose message contains 'locked' or 'busy' raised by a tick, rolls back the index's open transaction through a new public TelemetryIndex.rollback method, keeps the source fingerprint state it held before that tick, passes the error to an on_error callback whose default prints exactly one flushed line to stdout of the form '2026-10-02T18:30:00Z ingest tick failed: database is locked' (UTC time to the second, the message with newlines replaced by spaces), and continues to its next tick after the cadence; any other exception still propagates and ends the process; with a finite iterations count a failed tick counts as an iteration; cli.py is not edited; tests in tests/test_telemetry_ingest.py hold an exclusive lock on a fixture index from a second sqlite3 connection (BEGIN EXCLUSIVE) across one tick with a short busy timeout, assert that tick prints the failure line and does not raise, then release the lock and assert the next tick ingests the pending rows with none lost or duplicated, and assert a non-lock OperationalError still propagates; gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_telemetry_ingest.py tests/test_agent_ingest_cli.py tests/test_telemetry_index.py passes, uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes with exactly 1 test selected, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0; the gate log's first line names the commit it ran at, each command is logged verbatim beside its own summary and EXIT=N, and the gate runs in the foreground to its summary before the manifest is finalised",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Make the standing ingest loop survive a locked telemetry index instead of exiting",
